section: rts
synopsis: Fix DWARF unwinding information for ``StgRun`` on x86-64
issues: #27637
mrs: !16665
description: {
    A previous change that aligns the C stack to a 64-byte boundary in ``StgRun``
    on x86-64 (!15473) introduced an incorrect unwinding rule for ``rsp``.
    As a result, DWARF-based unwinders such as ``gdb`` could produce broken
    backtraces through ``StgRun``. This has been fixed.
}
